00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,140
He wanted a Congress full of cheerleaders.
他希望国会充满啦啦队员。

126
00:14:47,450 --> 00:14:52,418
And we had the naysayers and we had the hand ringers who were telling us that,
我们有反对者，也有人告诉我们，

127
00:14:52,418 --> 00:14:54,410
"Oh, you're fighting a fight that wasn't ours."
“哦，你正在打一场不属于我们的战斗。”

128
00:14:54,550 --> 00:14:55,490
And we were overreacting.
我们反应过度了。

129
00:14:56,890 --> 00:15:01,752
But we pushed forward and then the Voting Rights Act fell.
但我们继续推进，然后投票权法案就失败了。

130
00:15:03,170 --> 00:15:07,040
The pinnacle of the civil rights movements was gutted.
民权运动的巅峰被摧毁了。

131
00:15:08,079 --> 00:15:14,810
And in a matter of weeks, Republicans drew out black power all across the South.
几周之内，共和党人就在整个南方抽走了黑人权力。

132
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:21,840
And when the naysayers and the hand ringers came back and they told us that we didn't have the votes to fight back and
当反对者和手环者回来时，他们告诉我们，我们没有足够的选票来反击，

133
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:25,390
We were out of time, we didn't give up.
我们已经没有时间了，但我们没有放弃。

134
00:15:26,770 --> 00:15:33,490
We worked with the general assembly and we called a special session and the naysayers and the hand ringers.
我们与大会合作，召开了一次特别会议，反对者和反对者也纷纷召开。

135
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:34,710
They said, "Well, it's too late."
他们说：“好吧，太晚了。”

136
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:44,010
And I'm so thankful to our partners in the general assembly who passed the bill that then put it on the ballot.
我非常感谢我们在大会上的合作伙伴通过了该法案，并将其付诸表决。

137
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:52,720
And then the naysayers and the hamburgers, they came back and they said,
然后那些反对者和汉堡包，他们回来说，

138
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,380
"Well, listen, it'll never hold up in court."
“好吧，听着，这在法庭上是站不住脚的。”

139
00:15:55,600 --> 00:16:02,320
And then the Maryland Supreme Court voted by a 5-2 margin that they will allow it on the ballot.
然后马里兰州最高法院以 5 比 2 的优势投票决定允许该法案进入投票。

140
00:16:05,650 --> 00:16:08,030
And the naysayers and the hand ringers weren't done.
反对者和响手的声音还没有结束。

141
00:16:08,030 --> 00:16:11,290
And they said, "Well, you know, it's not polling well."
他们说：“嗯，你知道，民调结果不太好。”

142
00:16:13,650 --> 00:16:20,220
Well, thank God we ain't listening to them because we do hear the people of Maryland loud and clear.
好吧，感谢上帝，我们没有听他们的声音，因为我们确实听到了马里兰州人民大声而清晰的声音。

143
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:22,800
Loud and clear.
响亮而清晰。

144
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:27,300
And everybody do me a favor.
每个人都帮我一个忙。

145
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:36,850
Put up your threes in order to vote.
举起你的三分来投票。

146
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:42,610
Before us, people had to look down fire hoses and police dogs.
在我们之前，人们不得不瞧不起消防水带和警犬。

147
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:48,974
They had to look down police batons and the National Guard.
他们不得不蔑视警察的警棍和国民警卫队。

148
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:54,300
They had to walk past people who were screaming racial epithets at them.
他们必须走过那些对他们大喊种族歧视绰号的人。

149
00:16:56,380 --> 00:17:00,120
They did what they did in order to give us the right to vote.
他们做了他们所做的事情，以便给我们投票权。

150
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:08,180
And in order to keep it in order to protect our democracy and keep this in Maryland's hands,
为了保留它以保护我们的民主并将其掌握在马里兰州手中，

151
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,260
We didn't have to look down fire hoses.
我们不必低头看消防水龙带。

152
00:17:13,190 --> 00:17:16,172
We didn't have to stave off police dogs.
我们不必躲避警犬。

153
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:19,370
We just simply had to vote yes.
我们只需投赞成票即可。

154
00:17:23,199 --> 00:17:26,510
And that's what Maryland just did.
这就是马里兰州刚刚所做的。

155
00:17:33,323 --> 00:17:40,420
Maryland has always fought for this country.
马里兰州一直为这个国家而战。

156
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:49,215
In the free state, the state of General Harriet Tubman, the state of Frederick Douglas.
在自由州，哈里特·塔布曼将军的州，弗雷德里克·道格拉斯的州。

157
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:55,600
We've seen hard times before, but there have always been two things that have gotten us through.
我们以前也经历过困难时期，但总有两件事帮助我们渡过难关。

158
00:17:56,520 --> 00:18:00,200
God's grace and moral leadership.
神的恩典和道德领导。

159
00:18:01,417 --> 00:18:04,500
And frankly, we are going to pray for God's grace.
坦率地说，我们要祈求上帝的恩典。

160
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,780
And we are going to demonstrate moral leadership.
我们将展示道德领导力。

161
00:18:11,330 --> 00:18:13,450
That's what's going to get us through this moment.
这就是让我们度过这一刻的原因。

162
00:18:15,230 --> 00:18:23,250
It was the women who served as the greatest conductors of the Underground Railroad in the Eastern Shore who led their families to freedom.
正是那些担任东海岸地下铁路最伟大指挥的女性带领她们的家人走向了自由。

163
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:29,420
It was the union workers who prepared our nation for war.
正是工会工人为我们的国家做好了战争准备。

164
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:33,820
And it was the nurses whose hands healed a nation seeking peace.
正是护士们的双手治愈了一个寻求和平的国家。

165
00:18:34,529 --> 00:18:38,760
It was our sailors and our marines from Annapolis.
这是我们来自安纳波利斯的水手和海军陆战队员。

166
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:45,280
The ones who yell beat Army, which I have a very serious issue with,
那些大喊大叫的人打败了军队，我对此有一个非常严重的问题，

167
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:51,680
But the ones who live by the model, don't give up the ship.
但那些按照模型生活的人不会放弃这艘船。

168
00:18:55,160 --> 00:19:03,620
It was the young lawyers of the naacp who argued in front of the Supreme Court that separate does not mean equal.
全国有色人种协进会的年轻律师在最高法院面前辩称，分离并不意味着平等。

169
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:18,500
It was the ministers and the rabbis, the imams, the ones who left their pulpits and their mosques and their synagogues and their temples
是牧师、拉比、伊玛目、那些离开讲坛、清真寺、犹太教堂和寺庙的人

170
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:22,260
To provide comfort to those who had never seen it before.
为那些从未见过它的人提供安慰。

171
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:28,010
Every single one of them refused to leave anyone behind.
他们每个人都不肯抛下任何一个人。

172
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:33,810
And in this moment when too many Americans feel left behind by Washington,
在太多美国人感到被华盛顿抛在后面的时刻，

173
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,420
Our nation needs repair.
我们的国家需要修复。

174
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:47,080
And this can be and will be a moment when Maryland helps to save our country again.
这可以而且将会是马里兰州再次帮助拯救我们国家的时刻。

175
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:55,360
Because when our time is done, I want a Maryland where everyone has a shot to succeed,
因为当我们的时间结束时，我想要一个每个人都有机会成功的马里兰州，

176
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,620
No matter where their story begins.
无论他们的故事从哪里开始。

177
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:06,140
And where how much money your family has does not determine your value and does not determine how high you can climb.
而你家里有多少钱并不能决定你的价值，也不能决定你能攀登多高。

178
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:12,390
Four years ago, we started this journey together, y'all.
四年前，我们一起开始了这段旅程，你们大家。

179
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:19,690
And tonight, the work continues for our people, for our state, for our country.
今晚，为了我们的人民、我们的州、本州，我们的工作仍在继续。

180
00:20:20,559 --> 00:20:21,090
We love you.
我们爱你。

181
00:20:21,770 --> 00:20:22,770
I love you, too.
我也爱你。

182
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:29,200
So, in this moment, Maryland, let's work together.
因此，此时此刻，马里兰州，让我们共同努力。

183
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,440
Let's build together.
让我们一起建设吧。

184
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:35,400
Let's keep proving that a different kind of politics is possible.
让我们继续证明不同类型的政治是可能的。

185
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:39,380
Let's keep proving that we can lead in a way that the nation will follow.
让我们继续证明我们能够以全国追随的方式领导。

186
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:45,760
Let's continue to build a state that those who came before us hope for and a state that come after us for a state That they deserve.
让我们继续建设一个前人所希望的国家，一个后人所希望的国家这是他们应得的。

187
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:49,020
Let's make sure that together we will build.
让我们确保共同建设。

188
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:53,180
We will win and together we will leave no one behind.
我们将赢得胜利，我们将齐心协力，不会让任何人落后。

189
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:54,580
God bless you.
上帝保佑你。

190
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:55,820
Thank you.
谢谢你。

191
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:58,180
God bless the great state of Maryland.
上帝保佑伟大的马里兰州。

192
00:20:58,780 --> 00:21:00,640
And let's keep going.
让我们继续前进。
